TALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED as the default catalog source\" for units/IS_OFFERED_* flags), concept_department_dimension (decision guide: \"Use SIS_DEPARTMENT; it carries SCHOOL_NAME and IS_DEGREE_GRANTING\"), concept_cip_program_classification, concept_subject_offering_facts.\n\n**Column concepts**: column_concept_total_units (decision guide: unit statistics incl. geometric mean over catalog offerings → COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS), column_concept_department_name, column_concept_subject_id.\n\n### 2. Lineage & Relationships\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED joins → SIS_DEPARTMENT (DEPARTMENT_CODE), SIS_SUBJECT_CODE (SUBJECT_CODE), SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION (SUBJECT_CODE=COURSE); members of concept_course_catalog_sources and concept_subject_offering_facts.\n- SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION joins → SIS_DEPARTMENT (DEPARTMENT=DEPARTMENT_CODE), SIS_SUBJECT_CODE (COURSE=SUBJECT_CODE / COURSE_NUMBER), CIP (CIP_PROGRAM_CODE=PROGRAM_CODE).\n- Metric lineage: dw_4061 (geometric mean) ← COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED + ACADEMIC_TERMS; dw_1033 (CIP variance) ← SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION + SIS_DEPARTMENT; dw_2151 ← SIS_DEPARTMENT + COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED (same join as our geo-mean CTE).\n\n### 3. Similar-Entity Differences\n\n**3a. Catalog sources** (COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED vs CIS_COURSE_CATALOG vs DRUPAL_COURSE_CATALOG): all carry TOTAL_UNITS; only COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED is the documented default for `IS_OFFERED_*` flags and unit statistics (concept decision_guide). SUBJECT_SUMMARY/SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY are registrar-grain, lack IS_OFFERED_THIS_YEAR → NOT-SUPPORTED for \"offered this year\".\n\n**3b. Task-Requirement Fitness**:\n- Measure `TOTAL_UNITS` + filter `IS_OFFERED_THIS_YEAR='Y'` + `DEPARTMENT_CODE` → only COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED: SUPPORTED (column definitions retrieved).\n- `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING` for departments + `SCHOOL_NAME` → SIS_DEPARTMENT: SUPPORTED; STUDENT_DEPARTMENT: NOT-SUPPORTED (no degree-granting flag, per concept comparison).\n- `CIP_PROGRAM_CODE` variance + course-level `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING` + `DEPARTMENT_NAME` → SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION: SUPPORTED.\n- School name for combos → SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.SCHOOL_NAME: SUPPORTED (matches hint mapping).\n\n**3c. Wording-to-Field Anchoring**: \"degree-granting courses\" anchors to SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING (course-level, per hint) vs \"departments that are degree-granting\" anchors to SIS_DEPARTMENT.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING (department-level, per hint). \"Department of Management\" anchors to COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_CODE (hint) → code '15' (MIT Course 15 = Management; precedent dw_2151 excludes Biology via code '7', dw_1618 excludes Math via code '18' — same code-literal convention). \"Mathematics department (Course 18)\" anchors to SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT_NAME (hint). COURSE↔SIS_SUBJECT_CODE join: both SUBJECT_CODE and COURSE_NUMBER are documented; hint lists SUBJECT_CODE first and COURSE's own column desc names SUBJECT_CODE → use SUBJECT_CODE = COURSE (distinct school/dept pairs are identical under either join since ssc rows of a subject code share school/department).\n\n**3d. Precedent Usage Evidence**: geometric mean of TOTAL_UNITS: 1 precedent (dw_4061, on COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, `EXP(AVG(LN(...)))`). CIP variance for Math degree-granting courses: 1 precedent (dw_1033, VARIANCE() on SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION). ±X% ABOVE/BELOW/AVERAGE classification: 1 precedent (dw_3985, strict `> avg*1.1` / `< avg*0.9`). Per-group grand total with null: dw_12 (`WITH ROLLUP HAVING key IS NOT NULL`), dw_1350 (school rollup, null department). COURSE=SUBJECT_CODE join: 3 precedents (dw_3828, dw_3989, dw_2365); COURSE=COURSE_NUMBER: 4 precedents (dw_2398, dw_4756, dw_2639, dw_4490).\n\n### 4. Business Usage\nSIS_DEPARTMENT is the canonical filter dimension for degree-granting/school questions (concept decision guide); COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED serves catalog unit-statistics questions (37 metrics on SIS_SUBJECT_CODE family confirm heavy school/department rollup usage); SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION serves CIP and course-level degree-granting analytics (dw_1033, dw_1618, dw_2272).\n\n### 5. Coverage Checklist\nAll Phase-1 entities investigated: tables SIS_SUBJECT_CODE, SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION, SIS_DEPARTMENT, COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, CIP (semantic_get); CIS_COURSE_CATALOG, DRUPAL_COURSE_CATALOG, STUDENT_DEPARTMENT, SUBJECT_SUMMARY, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY (via concept comparisons); metrics dw_1033, dw_4061, dw_3985, dw_12, dw_1350, dw_1393, dw_2151, dw_2272, dw_3163, dw_1766, dw_1618, dw_2365, dw_2398, dw_4756, dw_2335, dw_3828, dw_3989, dw_2639, dw_4490, dw_3904, dw_1302, dw_1427, dw_1335 (semantic_get); concepts concept_course_catalog_sources, concept_department_dimension, concept_cip_program_classification, concept_subject_offering_facts (semantic_get/graph); column concepts column_concept_total_units, column_concept_department_name, column_concept_subject_id (semantic_get); graph: query_neighbors on COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, metrics_by_table on SIS_SUBJECT_CODE. **Note: mysql_query failed on every attempt (~15 tries) with \"Access denied for user 'root'@'localhost'\" — data-level verification was impossible; the SQL is grounded in retrieved column definitions and gold-metric precedents.**\n\n### 6. Recommendation\n\n**6a.** Combos: SIS_SUBJECT_CODE (SCHOOL_NAME) ⋈ SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.SUBJECT_CODE = SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.COURSE (DEPARTMENT_NAME), `GROUP BY ... WITH ROLLUP HAVING SCHOOL_NAME IS NOT NULL` (dw_12 pattern). CIP variance: VARIANCE(SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.CIP_PROGRAM_CODE) with IS_DEGREE_GRANTING='Y', DEPARTMENT_NAME='Mathematics' AND IS NOT NULL, joined to SIS_DEPARTMENT (dw_1033 pattern). Geometric mean per school: EXP(AVG(LN(ccso.TOTAL_UNITS))) over COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED ⋈ SIS_DEPARTMENT with TOTAL_UNITS>0, IS_OFFERED_THIS_YEAR='Y', sd.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING='Y', ccso.DEPARTMENT_CODE<>'15' (dw_4061 + dw_2151 patterns). Overall average = AVG of per-school geometric means (Tip #2). Classification: dw_3985 pattern with 1.05/0.95.\n\n**6b/6c.** Two-level aggregation (per-school geo mean → overall avg) satisfies the \"overall average geometric mean\" requirement; LEFT JOIN keeps every school/department combo; CROSS JOINs attach the global scalars. Data perspective: all columns verified to exist via semantic_get column definitions. Semantic-network perspective: concept decision guides uniquely select COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED and SIS_DEPARTMENT. Business perspective: each construct mirrors an existing gold metric precedent.\n\n**6d.** Tie-breaker note: COURSE_NUMBER=COURSE (4 precedents) vs SUBJECT_CODE=COURSE (3 precedents + hint order + COURSE column doc) — distinct combo sets are identical under either; chose SUBJECT_CODE per hint order. Management code '15' follows the MIT course-number convention evidenced by dw_2151 ('7'=Biology) and dw_1618 ('18'=Math).\n\nFinal SQL (6 columns, in asked order):\n\n",
